menu "EGOS SDK"

    config EGOS_ETHERNET_ENABLED
        bool "Enable W5500 Ethernet support"
        default n
        select ETH_USE_SPI_ETHERNET
        select ETH_SPI_ETHERNET_W5500
        help
            Enable W5500 SPI Ethernet as a network option.
            When enabled, the connection manager tries Ethernet first
            before falling back to WiFi.

            This pulls in the ESP-IDF W5500 SPI driver it depends on, so
            enabling this option is sufficient on its own. Without those
            selects, egos_ethernet.c fails to compile with implicit
            declarations of esp_eth_mac_new_w5500 and esp_eth_phy_new_w5500,
            and every consumer has to know to set them by hand.

    config EGOS_STATUS_LED_ENABLED
        bool "Enable status LED"
        default n
        help
            Enable the LED status indicator via LEDC PWM.
            Shows connection state through colour and blink patterns.

    config EGOS_STATUS_LED_MONO
        bool "Status LED is a single colour, not RGB"
        depends on EGOS_STATUS_LED_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            For boards with one status LED rather than an RGB one.

            Only egos_led_config_t.red_pin is used; green_pin and blue_pin
            are ignored. Every state and every pattern still works - blink
            rates, double blinks, triple flashes and the breathing pulse are
            all carried in timing and brightness rather than colour, so the
            only thing lost is the colour itself.

            States that differ ONLY by colour become indistinguishable. In
            the current state table that is the pair "connecting to the egos
            network" and "connecting to a stored network", which share a
            blink rate, and the two solid "connected" states, which differ by
            solid versus breathing and so remain distinct.

endmenu
